{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":156948,"name":"Sam Weber","username":"ssweber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/ssweber/{size}/9684_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-03T15:50:03.654Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ve read about the different “typo-squatting” attacks against PyPi, and was wondering if a delay in “registration of new package name” → “pip installable” could help?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI understand a day or 2 delay in publishing a new package name might annoy some people, but humans need to sleep, have days off, and such a buffer might make it easier on all those involved with alerting and taking action against malicious type squatting attacks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDisregard if there is already such a mechanism!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-03T16:20:34.161Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1046,"reads":137,"readers_count":136,"score":5257.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"Sam Weber","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":9414,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":156969,"name":"Juancarlo Añez","username":"apalala","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/apalala/{size}/683_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-03T19:18:27.979Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eMy understanding is that there’s an initiative to add namespaces to PyPi, so instead of:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003epip install alibrary\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would be:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003epip install trustednamespace.alibrary\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr the likes.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-03T19:18:27.979Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":134,"readers_count":133,"score":51.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"Juancarlo Añez","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":494,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":156971,"name":"Brian Schubert","username":"bschubert","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/bschubert/{size}/26920_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-03T19:30:37.130Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSome related threads:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"1609\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/b2d939/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/namespace-support-in-pypi/1609\"\u003eNamespace support in pypi\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ideas/6\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #3AB54A; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"Would you like to change something in Python? This might be your feedback forum.\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eIdeas\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    Elaborating on an idea initially surfaced in the \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/packaging-mini-summit-pycon-us-2019-topic-suggestions/1534/27\"\u003ePackaging Summit 2019 ideas thread\u003c/a\u003e and also mentioned at some point on the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/pypa/warehouse/issues/2589\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003ewarehouse github site\u003c/a\u003e, this thread is intended to capture thoughts on work needed to implement namespaces on pypi. \nI expect this could ultimately need discussed more broadly on relevant mailing lists. As someone that’s new to the PyPA ecosystem I’m totally open to suggestions about where best to communicate these ideas for feedback. \nThe basic idea is to implement support …\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"25552\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/debith/48/11937_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/too-similar-error-with-namespace-project/25552\"\u003e\"too similar\" error with namespace project\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/packaging/14\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"14\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #ED207B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"A place to talk about packaging Python software and the tooling to make that possible.\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003ePackaging\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    I am developing a library and want to release it on PyPI. It worked fine when I published part of the project under the name ‘pygim-common,’ but when I tried to release the ‘master’ project as ‘pygim,’ it failed because the names are too similar. \nBackground: \nI intend to use ‘pygim’ as the entry point for all other projects and ‘pygim-common’ as the main shared package with all other namespace projects. I understand that ‘pygim’ and ‘pygim-common’ have some similarities in their names, but how …\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"5090\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/polux/48/2602_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/improving-risks-and-consequences-against-typosquatting-on-pypi/5090\"\u003eImproving risks and consequences against typosquatting on pypi\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/packaging/14\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"14\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #ED207B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"A place to talk about packaging Python software and the tooling to make that possible.\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003ePackaging\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    [disclaimer: I write better in french than globish.] \n[disclaimer: forum’s stupidity force me to break most links.] \nHi, \nSome facts first\n\nI have recently been powned due to a typo in package name (request instead of requests).\nI wrote my story here (in french) : \u003ca href=\"https://metrodore.fr/i-have-been-powned.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003ehttps://metrodore.fr/i-have-been-powned.html\u003c/a\u003e\n\nThere is no CVE, no public statement about the malware. It is not found in publicly available database.\nThe trojan stayed on my machine during ~20 days after it was removed by the pypi admi…\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"4045\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/encukou/48/2461_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/pypi-as-a-project-repository-vs-name-registry-a-k-a-pypi-namesquatting-e-g-for-fedora-packages/4045\"\u003ePyPI as a Project repository vs. Name registry (a.k.a. PyPI namesquatting, e.g. for Fedora packages)\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/packaging/14\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"14\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #ED207B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"A place to talk about packaging Python software and the tooling to make that possible.\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003ePackaging\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    Hello, \nAs PyPI has become the de-facto canonical namespace for freely redistributable Python packages, I would like to encourage maintainers of packages in the \u003ca href=\"https://getfedora.org/\"\u003eFedora\u003c/a\u003e Linux distro to synchronize their \u003ca href=\"https://packaging.python.org/glossary/\"\u003eDistribution Package\u003c/a\u003e names with PyPI – effectively, to merge Fedora’s namespace into PyPI’s. \nThis has not yet been discussed in Fedora; I’m kicking off the discussion there as well. Here, I’d like to discuss the PyPI side of things. \nWhile this discussion is ongoing, the names that Fedora uses bu…\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-03T19:30:37.130Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":130,"readers_count":129,"score":66.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"Brian Schubert","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/namespace-support-in-pypi/1609","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Namespace support in pypi","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/too-similar-error-with-namespace-project/25552","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"\"too similar\" error with namespace project","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/improving-risks-and-consequences-against-typosquatting-on-pypi/5090","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Improving risks and consequences against typosquatting on pypi","clicks":0},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/pypi-as-a-project-repository-vs-name-registry-a-k-a-pypi-namesquatting-e-g-for-fedora-packages/4045","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"PyPI as a Project repository vs. Name registry (a.k.a. PyPI namesquatting, e.g. for Fedora packages)","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":22028,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":157020,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/7614_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-04T02:35:12.216Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThere is no current mechanism that I’m aware of for this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePyPI does have a separate, unrelated, mechanism for limiting “similar” package names: if a new package has an “ultranormalized” form that matches any other pre-existing package, it gets rejected. In practice, this means that you can’t upload \u003ccode\u003epy-fo0\u003c/code\u003e if \u003ccode\u003epy-foo\u003c/code\u003e already exists.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDelaying package visibility had come up a few times before (mostly in the context of allowing package maintainers to do “atomic” uploads or undo erroneous publishes without having to yank), and I think there’s general consensus that it could be useful. But nobody (AFAIK) has done the work to propose a design or actually implement it \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat being said, I’m curious how you think visibility delay helps with the typosquatting problem: I would expect most typosquatting to be opportunistic anyways, so the attacker can afford to be patient. Are you thinking that a delay would give the index’s admins more time tor review changes? This would be true, but I suspect the volume of new packages would overwhelm any manual review efforts. It’d need to be an automated process, at which point the security value of a delay is somewhat limited.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-04T02:35:12.216Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":113,"readers_count":112,"score":97.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":157056,"name":"Sam Weber","username":"ssweber","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/ssweber/{size}/9684_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-04T10:06:09.929Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"woodruffw\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"50195\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/48/7614_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e William Woodruff:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAre you thinking that a delay would give the index’s admins more time tor review changes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI got the impression from previous blog posts and incident reports like \u003ca href=\"https://status.python.org/incidents/dc9zsqzrs0bv\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://status.python.org/incidents/dc9zsqzrs0bv\u003c/a\u003e that sometimes these events happen in a very short period at opportune times (such as weekend), making it more difficult for the PyPi admins involved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA buffer might not help single malicious typo-squat package, but may help in the cases where hundreds or thousands of packages are attempted at once.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut I may not be understanding the scale of valid new package names being added everyday!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-04T10:07:58.253Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":90,"readers_count":89,"score":28.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"Sam Weber","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://status.python.org/incidents/dc9zsqzrs0bv","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Python Infrastructure Status - PyPI New User Registration and New Project Creation Temporarily Suspended.","clicks":12}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":9414,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":157158,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/7614_2.png","created_at":"2024-04-04T20:25:50.656Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ssweber\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"50195\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex016/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/ssweber/48/9684_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Sam Weber:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI got the impression from previous blog posts and incident reports like \u003ca href=\"https://status.python.org/incidents/dc9zsqzrs0bv\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://status.python.org/incidents/dc9zsqzrs0bv \u003c/a\u003e that sometimes these events happen in a very short period at opportune times (such as weekend), making it more difficult for the PyPi admins involved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey do, but I’m not sure (that’s not a negative, it’s genuine ignorance!) whether those primarily leverage typosquatting or whether it’s something else.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think my underlying concern is whether a package delay actually improves the remediation process, or just shuffles it around a bit – I could see it just as easily becoming a burden or DoS vector, where an attacker holds up the release of legitimate packages by filling the queue with spam.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-04-04T20:25:50.656Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":75,"readers_count":74,"score":50.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":50195,"topic_slug":"pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pypi-typo-squatting-is-there-any-mechanism-to-delay-new-package-name-visibility/50195/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_a